course: dictionary
lesson: 8985
title: One word, three meanings: site
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The word site has three meanings. First, a site is a place where something is, was, or will be, like a building site or a picnic site. Second, a site, or website, is a set of pages on the internet.
explain: «A shocking post that is on no trusted news site is probably fake.» Here the words trusted news and post tell you that site means a website. Third, to site something (a formal word) means to put it in a particular place.
explain: To choose the right meaning, read the words around site and ask: is this a place, a set of web pages, or an action of putting something somewhere? Then try your meaning in the sentence to check it makes sense.
fact: A site is a place where something is, was, or will be.
fact: A site, or website, is a set of pages on the internet.
fact: To site something (formal) means to put it in a particular place.
fact: «Building site» and «construction site» mean a place where something is being built, and they can be dangerous, so keep out.
fact: «Campsite» means a place where people put up tents.
fact: A «historic site» is a place from the past that people visit to learn about history.
exercise: «A girl in Ohio downloaded a cheat from a site that promised free gems.» What does site mean here? | *A website | A building site | A campsite | A historic site
exercise: «We pitched our tent at the campsite by the lake.» What is a campsite? | *A place where people put up tents | A school for campers | A set of web pages | A fast car
exercise: «Stay away from the building site, because it is dangerous.» What does building site mean? | A website about houses | A school for builders | A park with a playground | *A place where a building is being made
test: «The Carpathians are part of a World Heritage Site across several countries.» What does site mean here? | A building site | A sale | *A place | A website
test: The council will site the new library near the school. What does site mean here? | To paint | To delete | *To put in a particular place | To sell cheaply
exam: «When one site leaks passwords, criminals try them on other sites.» What is a site in this sentence? | A building site | *A set of pages on the internet | A campsite | A place where something is
